+// takes a pointer straight at __INIT_ARRAY__ (a plain, unprioritized
+// ".init_array" symbol crtbegin.o itself defines, holding a leading -1
+// sentinel) and does `while (*++list)`, i.e. it starts calling one slot
+// *after* wherever __INIT_ARRAY__ lands. The default GNU ld script always
+// places SORT_BY_INIT_PRIORITY(.init_array.*) sections -- which is what
+// init_priority(N) generates -- *before* the plain .init_array section, so
+// giving this constructor any explicit priority moves it in front of
